ASSISTANT Yes. From the technical report I can now see the encryption details:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - The cipher is **AES-128-CBC**
ASSISTANT - The encrypted PEM uses the **OpenSSL `enc` format**: `"Salted__" | salt (8 bytes) | ciphertext`
ASSISTANT - The PEM envelope headers are `-----BEGIN ENCRYPTED DATA-----` / `-----END ENCRYPTED DATA-----`
ASSISTANT - The passphrase (`random_secret`) is the **direct input to PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256**, not the derived AES key itself
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT This means the decryption command needs to use `openssl enc -d -aes-128-cbc -pbkdf2` with the passphrase from the file, rather than `openssl pkey`.
ASSISTANT 
